formatter: keep background-colored rows, unstyled blanks and hyperlinks in VT output

Three defects of the VT formatter, found by replaying its output into a fresh terminal and comparing
the screens cell by cell:

- A row whose only content is background color (erased with a colored pen, as every full-screen
  program with a colored background does) was treated as blank and dropped.
- A run of blank cells was written while the previous cell's style was still active, so the blanks
  after an inverse vertical bar came out inverse.
- Hyperlinks were emitted for HTML only; VT output lost every OSC 8 link except the cursor's.

Carried by ptyd against the pinned commit until it is merged upstream.

